        "original_id": "28a66407-9a08-50a8-81ed-02795b6678d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tie Domi, Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Bobby Orr, Max Domi\n- Organizations: Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment, Toronto Maple Leafs, Toronto Blue Jays, Ontario Raiders, Toronto Rock\n- Places: Toronto, Maple Leaf Gardens\n- Roles: Assistant General Manager, president, player\n\nFacts:\n- Tahir \"Tie\" Domi was born on November 1, 1969, and is a retired Canadian professional ice hockey player of Albanian origin.\n- Tie Domi played for the Toronto Maple Leafs.\n- Paul Beeston was a former president of the Toronto Blue Jays.\n- Bill Watters was the Assistant General Manager of the Toronto Maple Leafs.\n- Bobby Orr was a former NHL player.\n- Maple Leaf Sports & Entertainment considered purchasing the Ontario Raiders, but a group including Bill Watters, Paul Beeston, Tie Domi, and Bobby Orr bought the team for $250,000 instead.\n- The buyer group promptly relocated the Ontario Raiders to Toronto's Maple Leaf Gardens and rebranded the team as the Toronto Rock.\n- Max Domi's father is former Toronto Maple Leafs player Tie Domi.",
